{"course": {"id": "s16", "title": "Camday – Cambridge Primary Mathematics — Stage 6", "units": [{"n": 1, "t": "The Number System"}, {"n": 2, "t": "Numbers and Sequences"}, {"n": 3, "t": "Averages"}, {"n": 4, "t": "Addition and Subtraction (1)"}, {"n": 5, "t": "2D Shapes"}, {"n": 6, "t": "Fractions and Percentages"}, {"n": 7, "t": "Exploring Measures"}, {"n": 8, "t": "Addition and Subtraction (2)"}, {"n": 9, "t": "Probability"}, {"n": 10, "t": "Multiplication and Division (1)"}, {"n": 11, "t": "3D Shapes"}, {"n": 12, "t": "Ratio and Proportion"}, {"n": 13, "t": "Angles"}, {"n": 14, "t": "Multiplication and Division (2)"}, {"n": 15, "t": "Data"}, {"n": 16, "t": "The Laws of Arithmetic"}, {"n": 17, "t": "Transformations"}]}, "unit": {"n": 1, "stage": 16, "title": "The Number System", "strandShort": "Number", "blurb": "Place value in whole numbers and decimals up to thousandths, multiplying and dividing by 10, 100 and 1000, and rounding decimals.", "strand": "Number", "framework": "Cambridge Primary Mathematics (0096), Stage 6", "lesson": true, "subject": "maths", "read": "media/read/m6u01.pdf"}, "objectives": {"O1": {"code": "6Np.01", "sec": "1.1", "codeNote": "", "t": "Understand the value of each digit in whole numbers and decimals with up to three decimal places."}, "O2": {"code": "6Np.02", "sec": "1.2", "codeNote": "", "t": "Round numbers with up to two decimal places to the nearest tenth or whole number."}}, "sections": [{"id": "1.1", "title": "Place value", "objs": ["O1"], "lesson": [{"k": "hook", "t": "Race times", "p": ["In a swimming race, Leo finishes in **52.307 seconds** and Mia in **52.37 seconds**. The screen shows times to the thousandth of a second.", "Who won? What is the 7 worth in each time? Think about it before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Whole-number place value", "p": ["In 6248, the 6 is worth 6000 and the 2 is worth 200."], "qq": {"id": "m6u01s1t01", "type": "num", "prompt": "What is the 4 worth in 3485?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 400, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "400."}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Decimal places", "p": ["After the decimal point come **tenths**, **hundredths** and **thousandths**. Each place is worth **10 times** the place to its right."], "table": {"head": ["Ones", ".", "Tenths", "Hundredths", "Thousandths"], "rows": [["52", ".", "3", "0", "7"], ["52", ".", "3", "7", ""]]}, "p2": ["In 52.307 the 7 is worth 7 thousandths (0.007); in 52.37 it is worth 7 hundredths (0.07). Compare place by place: same tenths (3), then hundredths 0 < 7, so **Leo** (52.307) has the smaller time and won."]}, {"k": "idea", "t": "× and ÷ by 10, 100 and 1000", "p": ["**× 10** moves every digit **one place left**; × 100 two places; × 1000 three places. **÷** moves the digits **right**. The decimal point stays still; zeros fill empty places.", "**Decompose** numbers by place: 4.625 = 4 + 0.6 + 0.02 + 0.005. You can also **regroup**: 4.625 = 4 + 0.5 + 0.125."]}, {"k": "try", "t": "Value", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m6u01s1t02", "type": "num", "prompt": "What is the 8 worth in 6.184?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.08, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "It is in the hundredths place.", "reason": "0.08."}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I work with place value?", "p": ["Step 1: Write the number in a place-value table.", "Step 2: Read the value of a digit from its column.", "Step 3: × moves digits left, ÷ moves digits right (1, 2 or 3 places).", "Step 4: Compare decimals place by place from the left."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Multiply", "p": [], "q": "Work out 0.475 × 100.", "steps": [["digits move 2 places left", ""], ["47.5", ""]], "a": "47.5"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Divide", "p": [], "q": "Work out 62 ÷ 1000.", "steps": [["digits move 3 places right", ""], ["0.062", ""]], "a": "0.062"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Decompose", "p": [], "q": "Write 7.093 as a sum of place values.", "steps": [["7 + 0.09 + 0.003", "no tenths"]], "a": "7 + 0.09 + 0.003"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Missing number", "p": [], "q": "3.6 × ? = 3600", "steps": [["3.6 → 3600: 3 places left", ""]], "a": "1000"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Divide", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m6u01s1t03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 405 ÷ 100.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 4.05, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "4.05."}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Moved the point the wrong way", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "Work out 2.5 ÷ 10.", "lines": ["2.5 ÷ 10 = 25"], "bad": 0, "why": "Dividing makes the number smaller: digits move right → 0.25.", "fix": [["2.5 ÷ 10 = 0.25", ""]], "id": "m6u01s1t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "× and ÷ mixed up", "p": ["× 10 makes a number bigger; ÷ 10 makes it smaller."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Real life", "p": ["Sports timing uses thousandths of a second; scientists' scales show grams to 3 decimal places."]}, {"k": "summary", "t": "What to remember", "p": ["Tenths, hundredths, thousandths.", "Each place is 10 times the next one right.", "× moves digits left; ÷ moves digits right.", "Compare decimals from the left."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 720, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "1.1-k1", "t": 1, "after": 0, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m6u01s1k01", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Before you read on: who won?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "Leo (52.307 s)", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "Mia (52.37 s)", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}, {"id": "1.1-k2", "t": 2, "after": 4, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m6u01s1k02", "type": "num", "prompt": "In 52.307, what is the 7 worth?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.007, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "1.1-k3", "t": 3, "after": 9, "revie